{"id":"portswigger-web-security-academy--information-disclosure--common-sources-of-information-disclosure--authentication-bypass-via-information-disclosure","path":"portswigger-web-security-academy/information-disclosure/common-sources-of-information-disclosure/authentication-bypass-via-information-disclosure.md","title":"Authentication bypass via information disclosure","category":"portswigger-web-security-academy","source":"https://github.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/blob/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/portswigger-web-security-academy/information-disclosure/common-sources-of-information-disclosure/authentication-bypass-via-information-disclosure.md","html":"<h1 id=\"authentication-bypass-via-information-disclosure\">Authentication bypass via information disclosure</h1>\n<h2 id=\"description\">Description</h2>\n<p>This lab's administration interface has an authentication bypass vulnerability, but it is impractical to exploit without knowledge of a custom HTTP header used by the front-end.</p>\n<p>To solve the lab, obtain the header name then use it to bypass the lab's authentication. Access the admin interface and delete the user <code>carlos</code>.</p>\n<p>You can log in to your own account using the following credentials: <code>wiener:peter</code></p>\n<h2 id=\"solution\">Solution</h2>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Authentication bypass via information disclosure screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(27)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"Authentication bypass via information disclosure screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>Starting access to wiener user <a href=\"https://0ae80062039d9b5194f2429800130047.web-security-academy.net/login\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://0ae80062039d9b5194f2429800130047.web-security-academy.net/login</a></p>\n<p>Checking page sources there're not of interesting, so we can try access to admin page adding /admin path to our URL: <a href=\"https://0a160012030fde108045dab900300013.web-security-academy.net/admin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://0a160012030fde108045dab900300013.web-security-academy.net/admin</a></p>\n<p>and we can see this information disclosure message: \"Admin interface only available to local users\"</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Authentication bypass via information disclosure screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(28)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"Authentication bypass via information disclosure screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>so, we start to analyze request for understanding more things</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Authentication bypass via information disclosure screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(29)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"Authentication bypass via information disclosure screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>We can try to change request method to see if the answer changes.</p>\n<p>It will happen via TRACE method with the response status code 200.</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Authentication bypass via information disclosure screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(30)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"Authentication bypass via information disclosure screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>Trace is a debug method and it display us an important information as: X-Custom-IP-Authorization: 37.101.171.137</p>\n<p>We can copy it inserting a localhost IP: 127.0.0.1 in our request and change again method to GET</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Authentication bypass via information disclosure screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(32)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"Authentication bypass via information disclosure screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>Now we're into admin panel having the permission to delete 'carlos' user</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Authentication bypass via information disclosure screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(34)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"Authentication bypass via information disclosure screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>analyzing the reponse, there's a URL that permits to delete 'carlos' account: <code>GET /admin/delete?username=carlos</code></p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Authentication bypass via information disclosure screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(35)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"Authentication bypass via information disclosure screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>Copy and add it into our request to delete account and solve the lab.</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Authentication bypass via information disclosure screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(36)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"Authentication bypass via information disclosure screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Authentication bypass via information disclosure screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(37)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"Authentication bypass via information disclosure screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n","toc":[{"id":"description","title":"Description","level":2},{"id":"solution","title":"Solution","level":2}],"excerpt":"Authentication bypass via information disclosure Description This lab's administration interface has an authentication bypass vulnerability, but it is impractical to exploit without knowledge of a custom HTTP header used","searchText":"Description Solution"}